# AWOS CLI (`awos.py`)

## Structure

- `build_parser()` defines all subcommands (~line 1133)
- Handlers: `cmd_<command>` or `cmd_<parent>_<subcommand>`
- Default (no args): `cmd_guide`

## Command groups

| Group | Commands |
|-------|----------|
| `worker` | start, status, resume, diff, cancel |
| `mission` | guide, start, status |
| `sessions` | list, show, resume |
| `gauntlet` | list, run |
| Top-level | run, chat, budget, stats, report, index, goals, memory, traces, performance |

## Adding a command

1. Add subparser in `build_parser()`
2. Implement `cmd_<name>(args)` handler
3. Wire dispatch in main handler block
4. Add `tests/test_awos_sessions_cli.py`-style test
5. Live proof if user-visible: `scripts/demo_*.sh` + proof doc

## Dogfood safety

`awos.py` is in `.awosignore` — AWOS worker must not edit it during dogfooding.
